---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  title="About WhoRuled – data sources and licences"
  description="Where WhoRuled's borders and rulers come from, how reliable they are, and how to report a mistake."
  path="/about/"
>
  <main class="page">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">About WhoRuled</h2>
    <p>WhoRuled is a free interactive map of who ruled where. Move the year slider, click a state, and see its rulers, government and sources.</p>
    <h2>Where the data comes from</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Borders:</strong> <a href="https://github.com/aourednik/historical-basemaps" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">historical-basemaps</a> by Andre Ourednik, GPL-3.0. Historical borders are approximate; the source dataset has snapshots only for certain years, so the map shows the nearest one you select. Its last snapshot is 2010.</li>
      <li><strong>Present-day borders (2026):</strong> <a href="https://www.naturalearthdata.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Natural Earth</a> 1:50m countries, public domain. Made with Natural Earth.</li>
      <li><strong>Rulers and offices:</strong> curated entries (each with a source link and quoted words) and an import from Wikipedia's "List of state leaders" pages, used under CC BY-SA 4.0. State identities are Wikidata items (CC0).</li>
      <li><strong>Hierarchy:</strong> the overlord and subjects shown for a state come from the border dataset and are not curated.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>How reliable is it?</h2>
    <p>Every ruler, office, army figure and event links to its source. Army sizes are shown only with a citation and a confidence level.</p>
    <h2>Report a mistake</h2>
    <p><a href="https://github.com/nsijwali/WhoRuled/issues/new" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open an issue on GitHub</a> with the state, year and a source.</p>
    <h2>Open source</h2>
    <p>Code is MIT-licensed, curated facts are CC0 (imported Wikipedia rows stay CC BY-SA), the historical border geometry is GPL-3.0, and the present-day (2026) geometry from Natural Earth is public domain. See <a href="https://github.com/nsijwali/WhoRuled/blob/main/LICENSING.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">LICENSING.md</a>.</p>
  </main>
</Base>
